## 🧩 1. **Apereo CAS SSO Login Flow (Client-Side Example – Java Servlet)**

Below is a secure **Java-based servlet** snippet used by a university web application (e.g., LMS) to integrate with the Eduverse CAS server.

```java
// LmsLoginServlet.java
// Secured Web App: Learning Management System (LMS)
// This servlet handles CAS SSO redirect and validation

@WebServlet("/login")
public class LmsLoginServlet extends HttpServlet {

    private static final String CAS_SERVER_URL = "https://cas.eduverse.edu";
    private static final String SERVICE_URL = "https://lms.eduverse.edu/login"; // Must match registered service

    @Override
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)
            throws IOException, ServletException {

        // Step 1: Check if user is already logged in via a valid ticket
        String ticket = request.getParameter("ticket");
        if (ticket != null && validateTicket(ticket)) {
            // Ticket is valid — create session and redirect to home
            request.getSession().setAttribute("userPrincipal", "alex.student");
            response.sendRedirect("/dashboard");
            return;
        }

        // Step 2: If no ticket, redirect to CAS login
        String casLoginUrl = CAS_SERVER_URL + "/login?" +
                "service=" + URLEncoder.encode(SERVICE_URL, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        response.sendRedirect(casLoginUrl);
    }

    // Secure validation of CAS ticket (calls CAS server via service ticket validation)
    private boolean validateTicket(String ticket) {
        try {
            URL validateUrl = new URL(CAS_SERVER_URL + "/validate" +
                    "?ticket=" + URLEncoder.encode(ticket, StandardCharsets.UTF_8) +
                    "&service=" + URLEncoder.encode(SERVICE_URL, StandardCharsets.UTF_8));

            HttpURLConnection conn = (HttpURLConnection) validateUrl.openConnection();
            conn.setRequestMethod("GET");
            conn.setUseCaches(false);
            conn.setDoInput(true);

            int responseCode = conn.getResponseCode();
            if (responseCode != 200) {
                return false;
            }

            // Read the response: should be "yes username" or "no"
            try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(conn.getInputStream()))) {
                String line = reader.readLine();
                if (line != null && line.startsWith("yes ")) {
                    String username = line.substring(4).trim(); // Extract username
                    // Optionally: validate username matches expected pattern
                    return username.matches("^[a-z]+\\.student@eduverse.edu$");
                }
            }
            return false;

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("CAS validation failed: " + e.getMessage());
            return false;
        }
    }
}
```

> ✅ **Security Notes**:
> - Uses HTTPS throughout.
> - Service URL is encoded and registered in CAS server.
> - Ticket validation occurs via **CAS Server** (not client-side parsing).
> - Input validation on username prevents misuse.

