## 🔐 2. **CAS Server Side: Service Ticket Validation (Java CAS Server Code)**

This is the **server-side logic** in the Apereo CAS server (running at `cas.eduverse.edu`) that validates service tickets.

```java
// CasTicketValidator.java (Simplified, internal CAS logic)
public class CasTicketValidator {

    private final Map<String, Ticket> ticketRepository = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    // Validate a service ticket against the central registry
    public ValidationResult validateTicket(String ticket, String service) {
        if (ticket == null || service == null) {
            return ValidationResult.FAILURE("Invalid ticket or service URL");
        }

        Ticket storedTicket = ticketRepository.get(ticket);
        if (storedTicket == null || !storedTicket.isActive()) {
            return ValidationResult.FAILURE("Invalid or expired ticket");
        }

        // Validate Service URL against registered ones (CSP policy)
        if (!isServiceAuthorized(service)) {
            return ValidationResult.FAILURE("Service not authorized");
        }

        // Match ticket to the service
        if (!storedTicket.getService().equals(service)) {
            return ValidationResult.FAILURE("Ticket does not match service");
        }

        // Success! Return user info
        return ValidationResult.SUCCESS(
            storedTicket.getPrincipalId(),
