> 🔒 **Important**: Use HTTPS in production!

---

### 🔐 Best Security Practices Summary

| Best Practice | Why It Matters |
|---------------|----------------|
| Use HTTPS | Prevents MITM attacks and data leakage |
| Validate JWT/sessions per request | Prevent unauthorized access |
| Limit CORS to trusted origins | Prevent cross-origin leakage |
| Send heartbeats (`:ping\n\n`) | Prevent proxy timeouts |
| Avoid exposing sensitive data | Never send PII or tokens |
| Use unique event IDs and avoid reuse | Prevent replay attacks |
| Sanitize event data before sending | Prevent XSS (if injected in DOM) |
| Limit connection duration/number | Prevent DoS by aggressive clients |
| Monitor and log SSE activity | Detect abuse early |

---

### 🔍 Final Thoughts (From a Security Researcher)

SSE is **powerful but risky** if not secured properly. Always treat SSE connections like **any other authenticated channel** — enforce **authentication, validation, rate limiting, and input sanitization**.

> 📌 **Pro Tip:** Combine SSE with **rate limiting (e.g., express-rate-limit)** and **monitor connection counts per user** to detect abuse.

