## 📦 Step 2: Create a Basic REST API Using Node.js & Express

### 1. Initialize Your Project
```bash
mkdir secure-rest-api
cd secure-rest-api
npm init -y
```

### 2. Install Dependencies
```bash
npm install express mongoose cors dotenv helmet morgan bcrypt jsonwebtoken express-validator
npm install --save-dev nodemon
```

#### Why These Packages?
| Package | Purpose |
|--------|--------|
| `express` | Web framework |
| `mongoose` | MongoDB ORM |
| `cors` | Enable cross-origin requests securely |
| `dotenv` | Store secrets safely |
| `helmet` | Secure HTTP headers |
| `morgan` | Logging |
| `bcrypt` | Hash passwords (never store plain text!) |
| `jsonwebtoken` | Token-based auth |
| `express-validator` | Input validation |
| `nodemon` | Auto-restart on code changes |

