## ✅ Step 5: Secure Your API – Key Best Practices

| Practice | Why It Matters |
|--------|----------------|
| ✅ Use HTTPS (in production) | Prevents MITM attacks |
| ✅ Limit request rate (use `express-rate-limit`) | Blocks brute-force attempts |
| ✅ Validate ALL inputs | Prevents injection attacks |
| ✅ Never return detailed errors to users | Avoid exposing server info |
| ✅ Use environment variables | Prevent secrets from leaking |
| ✅ Use JWT with short expiry + refresh tokens | Reduce risk if token is stolen |
| ✅ Sanitize output (e.g., remove sensitive fields) | Prevent data leakage |
| ✅ Log suspicious activity | Help detect attacks |

> 💡 **Pro Tip**: Add rate limiting:
```bash
npm install express-rate-limit
```

```js
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');

const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100 // limit each IP to 100 requests per windowMs
});

app.use('/api/', limiter);
```

